// Hidden until every other origin is found. A lake on falling stones, a shaft an ember climbs, a road of vents and a hunter, a seed in a flame, the cancelling echoes again, a long crumbling bridge, a hunter before the door.
name Afterlight
rule B1357/S1357
steps 3
hidden
hint Everything at once: a lake on stones that fall, a shaft an ember climbs, a road of vents with a hunter on it, and at its end two echoes that cancelled, as in the warren. The seeds are on the way. One lies in a vent's breath.
tip Nothing new to deduce: the stones are two apart on the trench floor, one either side of the middle, each beside a lone floor cell. Everything else here is about staying alive.
intro You found all ten. The road has one more chapter, and it does not want you to finish it.
outro Eleven. Past this there is only the wall, and you already know what it says.
say wake|Stones over acid. Each holds for half a breath. Do not stop on one.
say seed|One. The other lies where a vent breathes. Count with it.
say plant|Two apart, as in the warren. You have done this before.
say grow|Watch the middle stay dark. Then up, and the long bridge, and the pale one.
say found|Cancelled and exact. The bridge past the vents falls tile by tile: run it. A pale ember waits before the door.
say die|This chapter counts its dead. Go again.
